Nephi Allred wrote:
>
> I have been a little out of the nethack loop for a while, but I recently
> got the hankering to make a new patch.
> I've decided to work on an idea that has been kicked around a lot: making
> some of the crappier artifacts more desirable. I did a quick review in
> Google groups to see what has been suggested in the past and also came up
> with a few ideas myself. So here are some thoughts, old and new:
> ...
> The easiest way to make these weapons a viable choice for players is to
> 1) give them abilities that make them useful in more general situations,
> and 2) make them more effective without needing the investment of scrolls
> and skill slots.

Agreed.  Except that they are fooproof.  I'd like to make all
the ways to get artifacts except #name to give fooproof.

> Some ideas for powers that would make the weapons more useful in general
> situations:
>
> For all banes: warning for target monster (like Sting for orcs).

I glanced at the code around this and it would be a reasonable
amount of work.  The method is already in place for Sting so
it is definitely doable so its a matter of effort.

> Demonbane: grant level drain resistance

This would make it competive with Excalibur.

> Sunsword: chance to blind opponent, increase light range to the same as a
> lamp

Camera effect.

If both of the above were done, I think non-Archon A's should
no longer get them.  As it is, if a chaotic character stays
in the dungeon long enough to face a lot of A's they get them
both.

> Giantslayer: grant 25 strength? (I don't really like this idea because I
> think that the banes shouldn't give the powers of the monsters they
> fight, but I can't think of anything else.)

I think it does make sense.  [oP effect already exists in the
code.

> Dragonbane: reflection. I don't think this is unbalancing given that the
> player must wield the weapon.

If this were true, it would make Dragonbane a valid alternative
in the broadsword family.  Reflection is something I value
enough that I'll take it redundant when possible, yet it is
rarely practical - amulet, shield, some quest artifacts.
Shields have enough other costs that i rarely use them.  It is
good Nethack cruelty to need to decide between Dragonbane for
redundant reflection and Magicbane for redundant magic resistance.

> Werebane: (already prevents lycanthropy). Negates effects of new moon?

Amulet of unchanging or ring of protection against shape
shifters effect when wielded.

> Trollsbane: prevent troll resurrection. (I know some people like trolls
> to come back, but they can always use a different weapon.)

Another Nethack cruelty - Make trolls killed by Trollsbane
not make corpses or not revive.  This would actually make
Trollsbane *worse* than its base non-artifact.  It would be
cool to have what on it's face seems to be an improvement
actually make matters worse.  Great trap for folks who don't
know about troll dancing.

> More tweaking:
>
> It's been suggested to change Dragonbane to a lance and Giantslayer to a
> two-handed sword. I like these ideas, but for this patch I want to avoid
> breaking bones/save file compatibility.

Dragonbane as a lance that does not break would make a
lance much better.  Truly wonderfull knight's jousting
weapon.

> Grimtooth could be poisoned. This would help out players in the early
> game, while being not very useful in the later game (since your tougher
> monsters are generally poison resistant).

It makes sense and it would make Grimtooth not junk
in the early game, junk in the late game.

I keep going back to artifacts being fooproof.  I want
most errosion damage to be able to continue to destruction,
and I want silver to be subject to coppper-like corrosion.
With those *decreases* in non-artifact weapons, the current
batch of artifacts becomes better.  Then make most other
ways that artifact generation happens make them fooproof
(found on the floor, MB held by archlich) while #name
continues as is.


